WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.450
The Harry Potter films were perfectly cast.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.070
But it's still fun to look at what might've
been, especially when it comes to actors who

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.870
decided to pass on the chance to participate
in such a huge blockbuster.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.680
Here are some actors who decided that appearing
in the wizarding franchise just wasn't for

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.200
them.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.840
Ian McKellen is a legendary actor.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:23.189
So it makes sense that his name came up to
replace Richard Harris as Dumbledore in the

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.170
wake of Harris' tragic death following the
second film.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.020
However, McKellen turned down the role because
he thought it would have been inappropriate.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.020
As he explained,

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.830
"People say to me, 'Don't you wish you'd played
Dumbledore?'

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.180
"I say, 'No!

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.730
I played Gandalf!

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:37.730
The original.'

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.120
There was a question as to whether I might
take over from Richard Harris but seeing as

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.480
one of the last things he did publicly was
say what a dreadful actor he thought I was,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.210
it would not have been appropriate for me
to take over his part.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.260
It would have been unfair."

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.540
"He played Dumbledore, of course, the wizard.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.400
I played the real wizard."

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.760
Although Michael Gambon eventually took over
the role for the rest of the series, McKellen

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.660
still gets confused for the character.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.370
He told the Telegraph in 2013,

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:05.300
"The other day there were 100 people outside
the theatre who wanted autographs.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:10.040
Just as I did the last one, a woman grasped
my hand and said, 'It's so wonderful to meet

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.400
Dumbledore in person.'

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.000
I blew her a kiss and got into my car."

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.740
Tilda Swinton was set to take on the part
of batty professor Sybill Trelawney, but she

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.460
ended up turning down the role.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.310
At the time, it was reported that she couldn't
fit the film into her busy schedule.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:28.540
However, some comments she's made since then
imply that she may have actually had a much

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.600
weirder reason.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:35.380
In a 2016 interview with Scots Magazine, Swinton
condemned boarding schools, Hogwarts included.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.560
She called her own experience at West Heath
boarding school in London a quote, "very lonely

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.030
and isolating environment."

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.030
She further explained,

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.020
"That's why I dislike films like Harry Potter
which tend to romanticize such places.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.560
I think they are a very cruel setting in which
to grow up and I don't feel children benefit

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.310
from that type of education.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.970
Children need their parents and the love parents
can provide."

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:59.620
Emma Thompson ended up with the part, and
Swinton avoided having to relive any bad memories.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.390
Hugh Grant was reportedly so prepared to play
the role of pompous Defense Against the Dark

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.469
Arts professor Gilderoy Lockhart in Harry
Potter and the Chamber of Secrets that he

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:11.569
went ahead and dyed his hair blond.

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:16.360
However, he ended up backing out to star in
the romantic comedy Two Weeks Notice.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:21.049
However, Chamber of Secrets director Christopher
Columbus contested these reports, claiming

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:23.540
that he had never spoken to the actor about
doing the film.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:29.019
Regardless of what Grant was or wasn't offered,
the part ended up going to Kenneth Branagh,

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.480
who brought his standard level of gusto to
the performance.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.260
Pulp Fiction actor Tim Roth was forced to
decide between Tim Burton's 2001 Planet of

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:40.519
the Apes remake and the part of Severus Snape
in Harry Potter.

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:44.870
According to Roth, he was offered the role
before Alan Rickman was, but he decided to

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.090
turn it down so that he could focus on Apes.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.450
As he told MTV News in 2007,

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.470
"I was going to do both films.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.500
We rigged it so that I could fly back and
forth.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.909
They figured out the schedule, but it just
got to be overwhelming in my mind.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.040
My kids really liked the books.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.849
They were really into me doing it, but the
idea of being an ape with Tim was too good."

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.349
While Rickman was ultimately incredible in
the role, Roth might've been closer to how

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:09.420
the books originally described Snape.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.579
Rickman was old for the part at 55 when the
first film was released, while Roth was only

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:15.380
38.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.120
Based on the books, Snape should've been 31
when Harry started at Hogwarts.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.540
According to Roth, he would've played Snape
very differently, but he ultimately believed

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.020
Rickman was the right man for the role.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.020
"I didn't want my life to be franchised."

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.040
Helen McCrory didn't miss out on the Harry
Potter films entirely, but she was kept from

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.749
playing a much bigger part than what she ended
up with.

00:03:37.749 --> 00:03:43.029
McCrory ultimately played Narcissa Malfoy,
though she was originally cast as Narcissa's

00:03:43.029 --> 00:03:45.260
sister Bellatrix Lestrange.

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:49.599
That role eventually went to Helena Bonham
Carter when McCrory got pregnant.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.800
"You should be honored, Cissy.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:51.600
As should Draco."

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:57.860
"He's just a boy."

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.720
As McCrory told Parade in 2011,

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.540
"I got pregnant with my first child, and insurance
wouldn't cover pregnant witches!

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.380
It was lovely that they invited me back and
wanted me to be a part of it somehow."

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:12.760
This begs the question, what are the maternity
leave policies at Hogwarts and the rest of

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.500
the Wizarding World?

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.160
Fans started pushing for author J.K.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.360
Rowling to appear in the Harry Potter films
as soon as they were announced, but the writer

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.720
says she's better off behind the camera.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:26.590
Rowling told the Sunday Mail that producers
offered her the chance to play Harry's mom

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.940
Lily, but she ultimately turned them down.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:29.940
As she put it,

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.980
"I really am not cut out to be an actress,
even one who just has to stand and wave.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.310
I would have messed it up somehow."

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.660
While Geraldine Somerville did a great job
as Lily, we're sure fans would've loved Rowling

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.720
in the part, too.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.500
Even if she did "mess it up," it would've
been a thrill to see a beloved author do a

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:45.020
cameo.

